This extension adds Red Dead Redemption modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Note that Magic RDR is required for some mods and will be automatically installed by this extension.[/summary]

[color=#d5a6bd][b][size=3]Loose file loading support is planned for KML. Once this is available, I will remove Magic RDR and update the installers to place loose file mods to be loaded by KML.[/size][/b][/color]

This extension will automatically install [url=https://github.com/Foxxyyy/Magic-RDR/releases]Magic RDR[/url]. It can be run from the Dashboard tab in Vortex and is required to install some mods. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/reddeadredemption/mods/164?tab=files]ScriptHookRDR[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/reddeadredemption/mods/291?tab=files]KML[/url] will also be installed automatically.

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Xbox[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]ScriptHookRDR mods with a "dinput8.dll" file and a "scripthookrdr.dll" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Kepmehz Mod Loader installs to the game folder, recognised by a "kml.asi" file.[/*]
[*]Magic RDR mods install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]MagicRDR Mod (Loose) mods with a ".wtd", ".was", ".dds", ".mtl" or ".wsc" file install to the "MagicRDR_Mods" folder.[/*]
[*]RPF File mods with a ".rpf" file install to the "kml\rpf" folder.[/*]
[*]ASI Script / Plugin mods with a ".asi" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]For upscalers, reshades, and other mods that need to be next to the game executable, please use the "Root Game Folder" mod type. This is the default mod installation path.[/*]
[*]Magic RDR will be automatically downloaded and installed in the root game folder.[/*]
[*]KML will be automatically downloaded and installed in the root game folder.[/*]
[*]ScriptHookRDR will be automatically downloaded and installed in the root game folder.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Red Dead Redemption mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

ScriptHookRDR:

Recognised when the archive contains a "dinput8.dll" file and a "scripthookrdr.dll" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

kepmehz Mod Loader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "kml.asi" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Magic-RDR:

Handled by the "testMagic" installer. Inspect the extension source for the exact archive layout it expects.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

MagicRDR Mod (Loose):

Recognised when the archive contains a ".wtd", ".was", ".dds", ".mtl" or ".wsc" file.

  Installs to: "MagicRDR_Mods"

========================================================================

RPF File:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".rpf" file.

  Installs to: "kml\rpf"

========================================================================

ASI Script / Plugin:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".asi" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]
